  "sourceAssessment": [
    "read_bounded validates cap before read, requests no more remainingcap+1, accumulates short reads toEOF, rejects overflow/protocol errors and preserves underlying IOexception identity; caller stream is never closed. It is a byte bound, not a walltime bound on arbitrary stream.read.",
    "parse_procs is limited4096B/64unique positiveu64PIDstrings; emptycensus preserved and incomplete/duplicate/invalid lists reject. It proves no ownership or livecensus consistency itself.",
    "parse_stat locates first PID/comm boundary and final closingcomm delimiter; selected positions are PPIDfield4 andstartfield22. Comm can contain newline/parentheses/bytes. Returnedtuple is partial identity only, not fullstat validity or a double-read/race protocol.",
    "parse_status bounds8192B and selected-field duplicates; requiresPID/PPID; NSpid is absentNone or1..64positivecoordinates with firstmatchingPID. RSS/HWM use exactkB and preserve absentNone. Repeated coordinates do not implyPIDreuse.",
    "parse_membership accepts one bounded unifiedv2 absolutepath line, rejects ambiguous records/NUL/CR, and returns exactbytes. No normalization/pathopening: later callers must compare to pinnedmembership and separately enforce safe filesystem ownership.",
    "Counter/event behavior retains previous review guarantees. No liveentrypoint, observation, path acquisition, sampling, SDK/process monitoring or installed dependencies introduced."
  ],
